The handbook is the document parents read in the portal alongside their child's progress reports —
rules, term dates, uniform, contacts.

**You need:** access to **Administration → Handbook**.

## Steps

1. Open **Administration → Handbook**.
2. Select **New section**. Give it a **title** first — saving without one gets you *Give the section
   a title before saving.*
3. Write the section's content in the block editor.
4. Save the section (**Section saved.**), or **save all sections** at once when you've been working
   across several.
5. Preview before publishing.
6. Select **Publish**, and confirm *Publish the handbook?*

You get **Handbook published (version _n_)** — the handbook is versioned, so each publish is a
distinct version rather than an overwrite.

## Drafts and publishing

Saving and publishing are separate on purpose. Everything you save is a draft; parents see nothing
until you publish. If you try to publish with unsaved edits you get **Save your changes before
publishing.**

So the working pattern is: write and save freely over days, publish once when the whole document is
ready.

## Deleting a section

**Delete "*section*"?** warns that **this cannot be undone**. It is a real deletion — there is no
undo and no draft copy left behind. If you might want the text back, move the content out first.

## What parents see

The published handbook appears in the parent portal. See
[Progress Reports & the Handbook](/docs/shared-parent-progress-reports).

